{
  "id": "WI-AJR-133-2022",
  "scope": "state:wi",
  "title": "AJR 133 (2021-2022 Wisconsin Legislature, regular session): requiring photographic identification to vote in any election (first consideration).",
  "urls": [
    "https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/2021/proposals/ajr133",
    "https://docs.legis.wisconsin.gov/document/proposaltext/2021/REG/AJR133"
  ],
  "version": "as-filed",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) Art. III, s. 1m (1) (proposed)\n(quote) [Article III] Section 1m (1) No qualified elector may cast a ballot in any election unless the elector presents valid photographic identification that verifies the elector's identity and that is issued by this state, the federal government, a federally recognized American Indian tribe or band in this state, or a college or university in this state.\n(b_no_id_remedy)\n(section) Art. III, s. 1m (2) (proposed)\n(quote) (2) A qualified elector who is unable to present valid photographic identification on election day shall be permitted to cast a provisional ballot.\n(c_mail_ballot_id) not stated.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule) not stated.",
